id: ki-sealing-handcuff
name: Ki-Sealing Handcuff
kind: gear
itemType: accessory
tags: tech
craftDC: Grandmaster
# "You may spend 3 Actions to place this Accessory on a Defeated Opponent or a Character with
# the Oblivious Combat Condition ... you must make a Skill Check (Stealth/Thievery vs
# Perception)." "If you possess the correct Key, you may remove this Accessory by spending
# 1 Action."
locks: true
lockCost: 3
unlockCost: 1
lockSkills: stealth, thievery
lockAgainst: perception
# The stack of Fatigued it holds on its wearer, and the mark that holds it.
sealCondition: fatigued
sealMark: ki-sealed
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Locked on a Defeated or Oblivious character for 3 Actions. Fatigued, and sealed off from
  Transformations, Signature Techniques, Unique Abilities, Ki Wagers and every Profile but
  Simple (Physical), until its Key opens it.
text: >
  Ki-Sealing Handcuff [Tech]: These handcuffs are designed for super-powered fighters,
  allowing them to be restrained even by weaker foes.
  –Craft DC: Grandmaster
  –Effects: When this Accessory is created, you must create a Key Basic Item for this
  instance of the Accessory. You may spend 3 Actions to place this Accessory on a Defeated
  Opponent or a Character with the Oblivious Combat Condition, even if they are already
  wearing an Accessory. In the case of the latter, you must make a Skill Check
  (Stealth/Thievery vs Perception) to put the Ki-Sealing Handcuff on them.

  While wearing this Accessory, you suffer from a stack of the Fatigued Combat Condition (that
  cannot be removed while you’re wearing this Accessory) and you cannot use any
  Transformation Maneuvers, Signature Techniques, Unique Abilities, Ki Wagers, or any Profile
  aside from Simple (Physical).

  While wearing this Accessory, you cannot remove this Accessory and you cannot target this
  Accessory with a Called Shot.

  If you possess the correct Key, you may remove this Accessory by spending 1 Action.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Given: with its Key, a Basic Item made with it that opens this one and no other.
#
# Lock on: the target, and 3 Actions. Defeated, it goes straight on. Otherwise the player
# says they are Oblivious by choosing Stealth or Thievery, and a Clash against their
# Perception decides it; the Actions are spent either way. On, it is theirs, worn past the
# two Accessories anyone may wear, with a stack of Fatigued held by the Ki-Sealed mark.
#
# While worn: it cannot be unequipped or thrown away, and the forbids below apply.
#
# Unlock, from the Key's row: the one wearing it targeted, or nobody for yourself, and
# 1 Action. It comes off them with the Fatigued it held, and back to whoever held the Key.
#
# --- What is not built -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Oblivious: no such Combat Condition here yet, so it is the player's word.
# Called Shot: nothing here aims a Called Shot at an Accessory, so there is nothing to refuse.
# Transformation Maneuvers and Unique Abilities: forbidden below, and read by whatever opens
# them when they arrive.
[passive]
forbid transformations;
forbid signatureTechniques;
forbid uniqueAbilities;
forbid kiWagers;
forbid nonPhysicalAttacks;
forbid profiles.nonSimple;
